@startuml
title UML state machine diagram for Inventory System

[*] --> InventoryHome

state InventoryHome <<choice>>
state AddGoods
state UpdatePrice
state RemoveGoods
state ExpiredGoods
state PlaceOrder
state GenerateInvoice
state SearchAndPurchase
state CalculateDiscountAndTax
state GenerateReceipt
state ReplaceOrCancelReceipt
state RecordCustomerRequest
state ViewSummaryReport

InventoryHome --> AddGoods : Add new goods
InventoryHome --> UpdatePrice : Update existing price
InventoryHome --> RemoveGoods : Remove goods
InventoryHome --> PlaceOrder : Place order to supplier
InventoryHome --> SearchAndPurchase : Search and purchase items
InventoryHome --> ViewSummaryReport : View transaction summary
InventoryHome --> RecordCustomerRequest : Record customer request
InventoryHome --> ReplaceOrCancelReceipt : Replace or cancel receipt

AddGoods --> InventoryHome : Goods added
UpdatePrice --> InventoryHome : Price updated
RemoveGoods --> InventoryHome : Goods removed

ExpiredGoods --> InventoryHome : Expired goods removed

PlaceOrder --> GenerateInvoice : Order placed
GenerateInvoice --> InventoryHome : Invoice generated

SearchAndPurchase --> CalculateDiscountAndTax : Items selected
CalculateDiscountAndTax --> GenerateReceipt : Discount and tax calculated

GenerateReceipt --> InventoryHome : Receipt generated

ViewSummaryReport --> InventoryHome : Summary report viewed

[*] --> ExpiredGoods : Expired goods detected
[*] --> RecordCustomerRequest : Customer request received
[*] --> ReplaceOrCancelReceipt : Billing process initiated

@enduml
